# PMD 0.6 feature tour

This notebook is both a program and a reader-facing decision document.

| Feature | Demonstrated by |
|---|---|
| Typed output | `produces=totaux:schema#totals` |
| Reader validation | `test-of=document` |
| Freshness | `stale-after=30d` |
| Rich tables | `display.csv()` with row dictionaries |

The following JSON fence is documentation, not an executable cell:

```json
{"tuiles": {"canada": 1600}}
```

## Scenario

```python {#scenario independent=true stale-after=30d produces=totaux:schema#totals}
settings = ctx.get("tuiles", {"canada": 1568})
tiles = settings["canada"]
endpoint = "https://tiles.example.test/catalog"
ctx.totaux = {
    "country": "Canada",
    "tiles": tiles,
    "storage_gb": round(tiles * 0.0045, 2),
}
print("metric       value")
print(f"tiles        {tiles:>5}")
print(f"storage_gb   {ctx.totaux['storage_gb']:>5.2f}")
```

## Cross-language consumer

```sql {#sql_summary depends-on=scenario}
SELECT
  json_extract(ctx_get('totaux'), '$.country') AS country,
  json_extract(ctx_get('totaux'), '$.tiles') AS tiles;
```

## Reader report

```python {#report depends-on=scenario}
totals = ctx.totaux
display.markdown(
    f"**Decision input:** {totals['tiles']} tiles require "
    f"**{totals['storage_gb']:.2f} GB**.",
    "decision.md",
)
display.csv([
    {"Metric": "Tiles", "Value": totals["tiles"], "Unit": "count"},
    {"Metric": "Storage", "Value": totals["storage_gb"], "Unit": "GB"},
], "metrics.csv")
```

## Document contract

```python {#document_contract role=test test-of=document}
assert "|---" not in rendered.text
assert "Metric\tValue\tUnit" in rendered.text
assert "Decision input:" in rendered.text
assert "tiles.example.test" not in rendered.text
```

## Conclusion

The source remains ordinary Markdown, while execution results are cached and
rendered outside the document.
